libSBML source code IS shipped inside this package, as the archive
src/libsbml-mod-5.21.0.tar.gz.  tools/cmake_call.sh unpacks it at build time,
builds it as a static library and links it into the r2sbml shared object, so
both the package sources and the installed binary contain libSBML code.

That archive is the official libSBML 5.21.0 release from
https://github.com/sbmlteam/libsbml with whole directories removed -- the
language bindings, documentation, examples, development tooling, autotools
build system, test suites, and the SBML Level 3 package sources this build
does not enable.  The files it does retain are byte-for-byte upstream.
tools/strip_libsbml_tarball.sh regenerates the archive from an official
release and documents exactly what it drops.

libSBML sources ARE modified during the build, after unpacking and before
compiling: tools/cmake_call.sh applies a set of patches required by CRAN
policy (removing calls to the system random number generator, output to
stdout/stderr, and [v]sprintf).  Those patches are applied to the unpacked
copy only; the archive itself is left as distributed upstream.

libSBML's own licence files are included in the archive and are installed
alongside the built library, at
src/libsbml-install/share/libsbml/LICENSE.txt (terms and copyright summary)
and src/libsbml-install/share/libsbml/COPYING.txt (the full LGPL 2.1 text).
Both are also available from https://sbml.org/software/libsbml/ and from the
libSBML source repository.

libSBML's main authors are Sarah M. Keating, Frank T. Bergmann,
Lucian P. Smith, Brett G. Olivier, Akiya Jouraku, Michael Hucka and
Ben Bornstein, with contributions from many others.

Note: libSBML also carries a copyright statement for the "SBML Layout" code,
(C) 2004-2008 by European Media Laboratories Research gGmbH (Heidelberg,
Germany).  That code is not compiled into r2sbml, because the build enables
no SBML Level 3 packages.  It would need to be listed here if
tools/cmake_call.sh were ever changed to enable them.


