8. Example SBML models
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Files:      inst/examples/*.xml
Source:     the worked examples in Section 7 of "The Systems Biology Markup
            Language (SBML): Language Specification for Level 3 Version 2
            Core, Release 2" (29 March 2019), M. Hucka, F. T. Bergmann,
            C. Chaouiya, A. Draeger, S. Hoops, S. M. Keating, M. Koenig,
            N. Le Novere, C. J. Myers, B. G. Olivier, S. Sahle, J. C. Schaff,
            R. Sheriff, L. P. Smith, D. Waltemath, D. J. Wilkinson and
            F. Zhang.
            https://sbml.org/specifications/sbml-level-3/version-2/core/release-2/

The specification carries no copyright or licence statement of its own.

  inst/examples/sbmlsimple.xml                            Section 7.1
  inst/examples/sbmlconversionfactor.xml                  Section 7.2
  inst/examples/sbmlconversionfactor-alternative.xml      Section 7.3
  inst/examples/sbmlassignmentrules.xml                   Section 7.5
  inst/examples/sbmlalgebraicrules.xml                    Section 7.6
  inst/examples/sbmlboundaryconditions.xml                Section 7.7
  inst/examples/sbmlmutlicompartment.xml                  Section 7.8
  inst/examples/sbmlfunctiondefinition.xml                Section 7.9
  inst/examples/sbmldelay.xml                             Section 7.10
  inst/examples/sbmlevent.xml                             Section 7.11

Every line of each file appears in the corresponding listing, except the
opening <sbml> tag of sbmlevent.xml: the listing in Section 7.11 closes that
tag before its namespace declarations, which is not well-formed XML, and the
copy here was corrected.


